### 0. Login as admin and customer
# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

# @name loginCustomer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 1. Create an event to book against
# @name event
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cancel Test Event",
  "description": "test",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2026-09-15T18:00:00",
  "venue": "Test Hall",
  "capacity": 5,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 2. Customer books 2 seats
# @name booking
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{event.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 2
}

###

### 3. Customer views own bookings
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 4. Customer tries to view ALL bookings -> expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 5. Admin views ALL bookings -> expect 200, includes the customer's booking
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 6. Confirm event seatsAvailable is 3 (5 - 2 booked)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{event.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 7. Customer cancels their booking -> expect 200, status CANCELLED
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/{{booking.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 8. Confirm seatsAvailable is back to 5
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{event.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 9. Cancel the same booking again -> expect 400 "already cancelled"
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/{{booking.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 10. Admin tries to cancel someone else's booking -> expect 403
# (re-book first since #7 already cancelled it)
# @name booking2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{event.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}

###

DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/{{booking2.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}